title: Where Claude runs
description: The outermost dimension. Which harness, which host, and what the chat is anchored to. It decides which of the other dimensions apply at all.
sections:
  - title: Harness, the two families
    description: The chat app and Claude Code read from different places entirely.
    body: |
      Before the merge there were three families: claude.ai chat, Cowork and Claude Code. The merge folded Cowork into chat, so there are two, and what Cowork used to be is now a chat anchored to a folder.

      | Harness | Reads from | Reach means |
      |---|---|---|
      | Chat app | The account: Settings > General, Settings > Memory, Settings > Skills, connectors, plus whatever the anchor brings | A Project, the whole account, or an anchored folder |
      | Claude Code | Files on disk: the CLAUDE.md chain, the rules folders, the skills folders, the settings tiers, the auto-memory index | A folder and everything below it |

      Rules exist only in Claude Code. Skills are the one kind that crosses the two: uploaded on claude.ai, they sync down to `~\.claude\skills\synced` and appear in Claude Code as one group.
    children:
      - title: Chat app
        description: claude.ai on the web or in the desktop app.
        body: |
          Nothing on this PC is read unless the chat is anchored to a folder. Standing instructions come from Settings > General, memory from Settings > Memory, skills from Settings > Skills, and a Project adds its own instructions, knowledge files and memory space.

          Owner still applies: a Project shared with people is the team's, a private one is mine, and an admin can provision skills for everyone.
      - title: Claude Code
        description: One engine, several hosts, the same files.
        body: |
          Every session starts by loading files from disk: the user CLAUDE.md, the CLAUDE.md of every ancestor folder down to the working directory, the repo's own CLAUDE.md files, unscoped rules, skill descriptions, settings and the auto-memory index. Path-scoped rules, subfolder CLAUDE.md files, skill bodies and memory topic files wait for their trigger.
  - title: Host, where Claude Code runs
    description: The host changes the tools on offer, not the sources.
    body: |
      | Host | What it adds |
      |---|---|
      | Terminal | The built-in tools and the MCP servers named in settings and `.mcp.json`. `/context` shows what loaded, `/memory` opens it |
      | Desktop app, Code tab | The app's own servers: a browser pane, a terminal pane, session and sidebar controls |
      | VS Code or JetBrains extension | Diagnostics, the current selection, diffs shown in the editor |
      | Cloud session | Runs on another machine. The repo's committed files travel; nothing from `~\.claude` on this PC does, so no user CLAUDE.md, user rules, user skills or auto-memory |

      Probe sessions run from the terminal and from the desktop app's Code tab saw the same eleven tokens, which is the evidence that the host does not change where instructions come from.
  - title: Anchor, what a chat starts with
    description: Picked in the chat picker. It decides what reach means in the chat app.
    body: |
      | Anchor | Sources expected |
      |---|---|
      | Nothing | Account-wide only: Settings > General, Settings > Memory, Settings > Skills, connectors |
      | A Project | The above, plus the Project's instructions, its knowledge files and its own memory space |
      | A folder | The above, plus file access to the folder, plus the folder's CLAUDE.md if the old Cowork claim holds, plus whatever survived of the per-folder instructions field and per-folder memory |

      Claude Code is always anchored to a folder, its working directory, so the anchor axis spans both harnesses with Claude Code pinned to one value.
  - title: Verified and pending
    description: What the probes have shown so far, and what they still have to.
    body: |
      Verified for Claude Code on 2026-09-20: every CLAUDE.md in the chain, the @import, both unscoped rules, the memory index and both skill descriptions load at start. Skill bodies, path-scoped rules, the subfolder CLAUDE.md and memory topic files do not load until triggered. The same set loaded in the terminal and in the desktop app's Code tab.

      Pending, each settled by one chat session asking "probe tokens?":

      - A folder-anchored chat reads the folder's CLAUDE.md.
      - A Project-anchored chat sees the Project's instructions and nothing from disk.
      - An unanchored chat sees only the account-level sources.
      - A memory saved in a folder-anchored chat shows up in a plain chat, which would mean memory moved to the account.
      - The plain terminal lists the skills synced from claude.ai.
